// Recorded gestures for the recogniser: what each sigil and sign looks like.
//
// ── EMPTY ON PURPOSE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The shapes belong to the manga. They have to be *traced*, not invented, and
// that has not happened yet. An empty list is an honest statement of that; a
// plausible-looking fire sigil would not be, and §2 of CLAUDE.md is explicit
// that an honest hole beats a plausible guess.
//
// `catalog.rs` already names every id this file may use — 13 sigils in
// `sigils.ron` and 35 signs in `signs.ron`. `templates::check` refuses any id
// that is not one of them, so a typo cannot quietly become a rune nobody can
// draw.
//
// ── FORMAT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//   version   must be 1; bumped whenever this layout changes, because a
//             recorded gesture is expensive to produce and a silently misread
//             file would be costly
//   id        a SigilId from sigils.ron, or a SignId from signs.ron
//   kind      Sigil or Sign — they are separate namespaces and nothing stops
//             the two sharing a name
//   strokes   one list of (x, y) per mark of the pen. Several marks are one
//             gesture; the recogniser never sees the boundaries between them
//             as ink, and never sees the order they were drawn in
//
// Units do not matter and neither does position: normalisation divides both
// out before anything is compared. Record at whatever size is comfortable.
//
// Rotation *is* kept, because canon rule 6 makes a reversed sign invert its
// effect. Record each shape the way up it is meant to be drawn.
//
//   (
//       id: "fire",
//       kind: Sigil,
//       strokes: [
//           [(0.0, 0.0), (12.0, 3.0), (20.0, 15.0)],
//           [(5.0, 10.0), (15.0, 10.0)],
//       ],
//   ),
(
    version: 1,
    templates: [],
)
